Subject: [PATCH] cmake: allow static builds on Substrate

The static-library build is gated to Linux only:

    if(SDL2COMPAT_STATIC AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
      message(FATAL_ERROR "Static builds are only supported on Linux.")

Substrate is an ELF platform using the same GNU toolchain and the same
versioned-shared-object conventions CMake implements for Linux (its
Platform/Substrate module defers to Platform/Linux outright), so the
restriction does not apply to it for any technical reason -- it is just
not in the list.

Substrate names its platform honestly rather than masquerading as Linux,
so add it to the match.  The SDL2 port this replaces shipped both
libSDL2.a and libSDL2-2.0.so.0, and dropping the static library would be
a regression for anything that links it.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@
 set(SDL2COMPAT_FRAMEWORK FALSE)
 #FIXME: should SDL2-compat modify vendor_info/revision information?
 
-if(SDL2COMPAT_STATIC AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux"))
+if(SDL2COMPAT_STATIC AND NOT (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME MATCHES "Linux|Substrate"))
   message(FATAL_ERROR "Static builds are only supported on Linux.")
 endif()
 
